description:
This plant was found in some dirt surrounded by a few rocks and trees in Tarpon Springs, Florida. This is a vascular plant with a reddish stem and yellowish green leaves that are grouped in fives. It is likely from the genus Parthenocissus due to its pointy yellowish green leaves and pinnate leaf veins. Plants of this genus are also native to North America and Southeast Asia.
@reenmath
Reference: https://www.discoverlife.org/mp/20q?search=Parthenocissus&guide=Trees&cl=US/FL&mobile=1

